From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:01:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_tonemap: add the bt2408_hable tone map

The new value maps HDR input to SDR BT.709 with the shared bt2408_hable
helper. The peak comes from the content light level or the mastering
display side data, as for the other curves, and the helper is rebuilt
only when the peak or the primaries change. The output is tagged
BT.709 and drops the light level side data, since it no longer
describes the frame. The existing curves are untouched.

The test runs the filter in a graph on the helper's test colours and
checks the peak from MaxCLL, the peak from the mastering display, the
output tags and a planted wrong MaxCLL.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 doc/filters.texi                           |  18 +++
 libavfilter/Makefile                       |   2 +-
 libavfilter/tests/bt2408_hable.c           | 146 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 libavfilter/vf_tonemap.c                   | 102 +++++++++++---
 tests/fate/filter-video.mak                |   4 +
 tests/ref/fate/filter-tonemap-bt2408-hable |   4 +
 6 files changed, 256 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/ref/fate/filter-tonemap-bt2408-hable

diff --git a/doc/filters.texi b/doc/filters.texi
index 1c29a51458b99c37b541946dc15497d47028e9ac..06e09698a80ffd28c9c9b949c163976958604132 100644
--- a/doc/filters.texi
+++ b/doc/filters.texi
@@ -24248,6 +24248,12 @@ data should be linearized beforehand (and possibly correctly tagged).
 ffmpeg -i INPUT -vf zscale=transfer=linear,tonemap=clip,zscale=transfer=bt709,format=yuv420p OUTPUT
 @end example
 
+Tone map a Dolby Vision profile 5 or an HDR10 input to SDR BT.709:
+@example
+ffmpeg -i INPUT -vf dovi_reshape,zscale=transfer=linear,format=gbrpf32le,tonemap=bt2408_hable,zscale=transfer=bt709:matrix=bt709:range=tv,format=yuv420p OUTPUT
+@end example
+For HDR10 input, leave out @code{dovi_reshape}.
+
 @subsection Options
 The filter accepts the following options.
 
@@ -24283,6 +24289,18 @@ important than color and brightness accuracy.
 Smoothly map out-of-range values, while retaining contrast and colors for
 in-range material as much as possible. Use it when color accuracy is more
 important than detail preservation.
+
+@item bt2408_hable
+Map HDR input to SDR BT.709 the way libplacebo does with its @code{hable}
+tone mapping and clipping gamut mapping: the Hable curve is applied to the
+intensity of IPT, with the SDR reference white at 203 cd/m^2 (ITU-R BT.2408),
+and chroma is reduced as the curve compresses intensity. The input must use
+D65 primaries, with 1.0 = 100 cd/m^2 as @ref{zscale} produces with its default
+@option{npl}. The output is in BT.709 primaries and tagged as such, still in
+linear light, so that a following @code{zscale=transfer=bt709} encodes it for
+a BT.1886 display with a 1000:1 contrast. The content light level and
+mastering display side data are dropped from the output. The options
+@option{param} and @option{desat} are ignored.
 @end table
 
 Default is none.
